<title>CHINA: Pioneer Industries yr net down 13.19 pct.</title>
<headline>Pioneer Industries yr net down 13.19 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   22.65	vs 27.73</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    8.0	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  20.19 loss vs 4.39 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    73.65	vs 84.85</p>
<p>    Turnover		     115.23     vs 89.68</p>
<p>    Company name		 Pioneer Industries International</p>
<p>				     (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 22-26</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 15</p>
<p>NOTE - Pioneer Industries engages in property investments and development. It also has interests in hotels and securities.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss on provision for diminution - marketable securities, write off of long term investment, payment to a bank on liquidation of a textile mill in Malaysia formerly held by an associate and legal fees, including defendant's legal cost and interest thereon, and other fees in respect of the sale of a hotel in Malaysia in 1990.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is eight H.K. cents vs six cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
